  "hardware": [
    {
      "item": "Braided line for tendons",
      "qty": 10,
      "note": "one flexor and one extensor run per finger; length to suit the print"
    },
    {
      "item": "PTFE tube (tendon sheath)",
      "qty": 1,
      "note": "cut into one sheath per tendon run through the wrist"
    },
    {
      "item": "Elastic cord or torsion spring (finger return)",
      "qty": 5
    },
    {
      "item": "M2 screw (servo tabs)",
      "qty": 12,
      "note": "usually supplied with the SG90"
    },
    {
      "item": "Steel pin or M2 screw (finger hinge axle)",
      "qty": 14,
      "note": "one per finger joint"
    },
    {
      "item": "608 ball bearing (wrist)",
      "qty": 1,
      "note": "standard 8 × 22 × 7 mm bearing"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Kinematics only: each finger's middle and distal joints follow its knuckle by fixed ratios, which stands in for the tendon; grip force, tendon stretch and friction are not simulated.",
    "Six SG90s draw far more than the Uno's USB fuse allows when they move together; the template powers them from a 5 V bench supply with a ground shared with the Uno.",
    "Assembly: print the phalanges and palm, thread each flexor from its servo horn through a PTFE sheath and the palm channel to the fingertip, add the return elastic on the back of the finger."
  ]
}
